Swedish-keyword Scala toolchain for Kojo — a STUB
=================================================

This directory is a starting point for a Swedish edition of Kojo at the deepest
level of localization (Level 4 in ../localization.md): programming in Swedish
*keywords*, e.g. `värde x = 5` instead of `val x = 5`.

It mirrors the Turkish work in ../scala-tr/. Nothing here is built or wired in
yet — it is meant to save the Swedish contributors the reverse-engineering, not
to be a finished feature.

What is here
------------
* swedish-keywords.patch — the compiler patch (see below). VERIFIED to apply
  cleanly to a pristine scala/scala v2.13.18 checkout.
* scalariform-swedish.patch — the code-formatter/highlighter patch (see below).
  VERIFIED to apply cleanly to bulent2k2/scalariform. Uses the same Swedish
  words as the compiler patch.
* KEYWORDS.md — the draft English→Swedish keyword table, with the words that
  need the most care called out. READ THIS FIRST.

*** The Swedish words are AI-suggested drafts. A native Swedish speaker must
    review them before anything is built. *** Neither the author of this stub
    nor the Kojo maintainers speak Swedish; the value here is the mechanism,
    not the word choices.

Building the patched compiler
-----------------------------
Exactly as for Turkish (see ../scala-tr/README):

    git clone https://github.com/scala/scala ~/src/scala-2.13.18
    cd ~/src/scala-2.13.18 && git checkout v2.13.18
    git apply <kojo-clone>/scala-sv/swedish-keywords.patch
    # Java 8 or 11 on PATH (the Scala 2.13 build wants it)
    sbt 'set Global/baseVersionSuffix := ""' dist/mkPack   # ~3 minutes

The `baseVersionSuffix := ""` is the fix that gives the jars a clean
`version.number=2.13.18` (see ../scala-tr/README for why it matters).

`build/pack/lib/{scala-library,scala-reflect,scala-compiler}.jar` are then the
Swedish toolchain. Publish them the way the Turkish jars are published — a
GitHub release of a scala fork, consumed on demand by Kojo — see
../scala-tr/README and the ScalaToolchainFetcher in the Kojo source.

Building the Swedish scalariform
--------------------------------
Kojo's editor formats and highlights code with scalariform, which keeps its own
keyword table, so a fourth jar in the release must know the Swedish keywords:

    git clone https://github.com/bulent2k2/scalariform ~/src/scalariform-sv
    cd ~/src/scalariform-sv
    git apply <kojo-clone>/scala-sv/scalariform-swedish.patch
    sbt packageBin                 # see the fork's Makefile / README_bulent2k2
    # -> scalariform/target/scala-2.13/scalariform_2.13-0.2.10.jar

Rename that jar to `scalariform.jar` in the release. Use `packageBin` (the slim
~1.2 MB library jar), NOT `assembly` (a fat CLI jar with a bundled scala-library).
Sanity-check: `unzip -l scalariform.jar | grep -c scala/collection/` should be 0.
(bulent2k2/scalariform already carries the Turkish keywords, so the resulting jar
recognizes English, Turkish and Swedish; a Swedish user only ever sees Swedish
highlighted, and scalariform-swedish.patch reproduces just the Swedish delta on
top of that fork, not on pristine upstream scalariform.)

The on-demand fetcher requires all four jars — scala-library, scala-reflect,
scala-compiler and scalariform — plus a SHA256SUMS, in the release, or it
refuses the whole toolchain and falls back to stock.

The patch touches the same three files as the Turkish one, and only adds:
    Main.scala      one diagnostic println (optional)
    Scanners.scala  the Swedish keyword entries, FIRST in allKeywords so that
                    compiler errors still report the English keyword
    StdNames.scala  the Swedish keyword strings

Status of the four Level-4 pieces (see ../localization.md)
----------------------------------------------------------
  1. Patched compiler ............ swedish-keywords.patch (here) — build & publish
  2. Runtime toolchain toggle .... DONE, language-agnostic. `sv` is registered
                                   in ScalaToolchain.keywordLanguages and the
                                   fetcher pulls v<ver>-sv on demand. Nothing
                                   Swedish-specific to write.
  3. Code formatting (scalariform) scalariform-swedish.patch (here) — build the
                                   4th release jar as above.
  4. Syntax highlighting ......... DONE via i18n.KeywordLangs, which is now
                                   registered for `sv` (i18n/sv/package.scala).

What still needs a native Swedish speaker
-----------------------------------------
* Review/replace the AI-drafted words in KEYWORDS.md (edit both patches).
* A Swedish Level-1/2 API and samples, and keyword-completion templates
  (i18n/sv/package.scala currently leaves the template maps empty).
